  "claim": "Mathematician, Victor Borisovich Lidskii , had an adviser at Moscow State University. His Italian advisor was born after Mykhailo Pylypovych Kravchuk.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Mikhail Kravchuk. Sentence: Mykhailo Pylypovych Kravchuk, also Krawtchouk (Ukrainian: Миха́йло Пили́пович Кравчу́к ) (September 27, 1892 – March 9, 1942), was a Soviet Ukrainian mathematician who, despite his early death, was the author of around 180 articles on mathematics.\nPage: Israel Gelfand. Sentence: Israel Moiseevich Gelfand, also written Israïl Moyseyovich Gel'fand, or Izrail M. Gelfand (Yiddish: ישראל געלפֿאַנד‎ , Russian: Изра́иль Моисе́евич Гельфа́нд ; 2 September [O.S. 20 August] 1913 – 5 October 2009) was a prominent Soviet mathematician.\nPage: Victor Lidskii. Sentence: His adviser at Moscow State University was Israel Gelfand.",
