        "original_id": "ac18b18c-5862-50a6-b114-a7d4d7378f12",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mykhailo Pylypovych Kravchuk, Israel Moiseevich Gelfand, Victor Lidskii\n- Organizations: Moscow State University\n- Roles: Mathematicians, adviser\n\nFacts:\n- Mykhailo Pylypovych Kravchuk, also known as Krawtchouk, was a Soviet Ukrainian mathematician who lived from September 27, 1892 to March 9, 1942.\n- Mykhailo Pylypovych Kravchuk authored around 180 articles on mathematics despite his early death.\n- Israel Moiseevich Gelfand, also written as Israïl Moyseyovich Gel'fand or Izrail M. Gelfand, was a prominent Soviet mathematician who lived from 2 September 1913 to 5 October 2009.\n- Israel Gelfand was the adviser of Victor Lidskii at Moscow State University.",
